    "notes": "Volcanic badlands: grey ash dunes over black basalt, charred snags, yellow brimstone crusts and the magenta of fireweed, the first plant back on any burn. Geothermally warm (day 42, night 22) and dry. The ash is a POWDER skin, so basalt is its firm skin: every slope past the ash's repose and every cut face is black rock. Caves are lava tubes (more of them, no mushrooms). Treeline 1.8x the map's so the cones stay bare ash, not snow."
